---
import AboutArticle from "../../components/AboutArticle.astro";
import { affiliateHref, commerceLinkRel } from "../../lib/affiliateLinks";
import { BOM } from "../../lib/bomLinks";
import { getAboutPage } from "../../lib/aboutPages";
import { getAboutHeroPhoto } from "../../lib/aboutPhotos";

const page = getAboutPage("cellular-ingest")!;
const hero = getAboutHeroPhoto(page.slug);

const PARTICLE_BORON = affiliateHref("https://www.particle.io/wifi/#boron");
const AMAZON_BORON = BOM.amazonBoronSearch;
const ADAFRUIT_DS18B20 = BOM.adafruitDs18b20;
const AMAZON_DS18B20 = BOM.amazonDs18b20;
const AMAZON_RESISTOR = BOM.amazonResistor4k7;
const BLUES_NOTECARD = affiliateHref("https://blues.io/products/notecard/");
---
<AboutArticle
  slug={page.slug}
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  heroImage={hero?.image}
  heroAlt={hero?.alt}
  heroCaption={hero?.caption}
  heroCredit={hero?.credit}
  heroCreditHref={hero?.sourceUrl}
  commerceDisclosure
>
  <p>
    Cabins, wells, and outbuildings often have power but no garage Wi‑Fi. A
    <strong>Particle Boron</strong> (or B-Series) LTE board POSTs the same ingest JSON through a
    <strong>Particle Console webhook</strong>. Cellular dropouts are normal: ThermalTrace already
    marks probes stale when posts stop, so you do not need an aggressive on-device retry storm.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prefer Blues? A <strong>Notecard</strong> + Notehub route can forward the same JSON; the Boron
    sketch is the first-class download from Devices.
  </p>

  <h2>Parts</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
    <table class="plan-comparison-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">Parts for a cellular freeze probe</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Part</th>
          <th scope="col">Why</th>
          <th scope="col">Buy</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Particle Boron / B-Series</th>
          <td>LTE-M / NB-IoT (region SKU). Nano-SIM or Particle SIM plan required.</td>
          <td>
            <a class="text-link" href={PARTICLE_BORON} target="_blank" rel={commerceLinkRel(PARTICLE_BORON)}>Particle Boron</a>
            ·
            <a class="text-link" href={AMAZON_BORON} target="_blank" rel={commerceLinkRel(AMAZON_BORON)}>Amazon search</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Waterproof DS18B20</th>
          <td>Pipe / crawlspace probe. Data on <strong>D2</strong>.</td>
          <td>
            <a class="text-link" href={ADAFRUIT_DS18B20} target="_blank" rel={commerceLinkRel(ADAFRUIT_DS18B20)}>Adafruit DS18B20</a>
            ·
            <a class="text-link" href={AMAZON_DS18B20} target="_blank" rel={commerceLinkRel(AMAZON_DS18B20)}>Amazon</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">4.7kΩ resistor</th>
          <td>Pull-up from DS18B20 data to 3.3V.</td>
          <td>
            <a class="text-link" href={AMAZON_RESISTOR} target="_blank" rel={commerceLinkRel(AMAZON_RESISTOR)}>Amazon 4.7k</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Cellular plan</th>
          <td>Particle cloud + carrier data. Budget for remote sites that only wake hourly.</td>
          <td>Particle Console billing or your own nano-SIM where the SKU allows it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Optional: Blues Notecard</th>
          <td>Alternate cellular path via Notehub webhook route (same ingest URL).</td>
          <td>
            <a class="text-link" href={BLUES_NOTECARD} target="_blank" rel={commerceLinkRel(BLUES_NOTECARD)}>Blues Notecard</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Wiring</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>DS18B20 VDD → Boron <strong>3V3</strong></li>
    <li>DS18B20 GND → GND</li>
    <li>DS18B20 data → <strong>D2</strong>, 4.7k to 3V3</li>
    <li>USB for flash and 115200 serial; antenna attached before field deploy</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Flash and webhook</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open
      <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/devices">Dashboard → Devices</a>
      and download <strong>Particle Boron .ino</strong> plus the webhook JSON (ingest URL filled in).
    </li>
    <li>
      Flash with Particle Workbench or Web IDE (Device OS 5+). Libraries:
      <code>OneWire</code>, <code>spark-dallas-temperature</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Console → Integrations → Webhook: event <code>thermaltrace_ingest</code>, POST to your ingest URL,
      use the downloaded webhook JSON (or set the body to the Particle event value), Content-Type
      <code>application/json</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Serial 115200: <code>publish ok</code>. Webhook history should show HTTP 200. Sensor key
      <code>temp1</code> imports on first successful POST.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Repo listing:
    <a
      class="text-link"
      href="https://github.com/doodersrage/thermaltrace/tree/main/sketches/particle/boron_ds18b20_ingest"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer"
    ><code>sketches/particle/boron_ds18b20_ingest/</code></a>
  </p>

  <h2>Dropouts and stale probes</h2>
  <p>
    LTE will miss intervals in weather, roaming, or prepaid outages. Keep posting about once a minute when
    connected; let
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/debugging-stale-readings">stale-reading detection</a>
    and freeze alerts cover silence. Do not burn battery on tight reconnect loops.
  </p>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a class="text-link" href="/about/adding-devices">Adding devices</a></li>
    <li><a class="text-link" href="/about/debugging-stale-readings">Debugging stale readings</a></li>
    <li><a class="text-link" href="/about/teensy41-ingest">Teensy 4.1 Ethernet</a></li>
    <li><a class="text-link" href="/about/pic18-ethernet-ingest">PIC18F67J60 Ethernet</a></li>
    <li>
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://github.com/doodersrage/thermaltrace/tree/main/sketches"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >All sketches ↗</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</AboutArticle>
